WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.334 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Our next guest
is a Tony-nominated

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.736 align:start size:94% position:6%
and Emmy Award-winning actress
you know

00:00:02.736 --> 00:00:05.538 align:start size:94% position:6%
from films such as "The Truman
Show" and "Legally Blonde"

00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:08.508
and shows such as "The Practice"
and "Two and a Half Men."

00:00:08.508 --> 00:00:10.210 align:start size:94% position:6%
She's currently starring
in "The Stand In,"

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:13.013
which is in select theaters,
on demand, and on digital now.

00:00:13.013 --> 00:00:16.049
Please welcome to the show
Holland Taylor, everybody.

00:00:16.049 --> 00:00:17.283 size:78% position:39% line:92%
How are you, Holland?

00:00:17.283 --> 00:00:18.084 line:92%
-I'm thrilled to be here.

00:00:18.084 --> 00:00:20.086 align:start size:94% position:6%
I can't believe I've never
been on your show.

00:00:20.086 --> 00:00:21.454 line:92%
I'm so glad to see you this way.

00:00:21.454 --> 00:00:24.124
-I know. I am both thrille
that you're finally here

00:00:24.124 --> 00:00:25.525 align:start size:94% position:6%
and heartbroken
it's not in person.

00:00:25.525 --> 00:00:29.362
It has been a very long time
since I saw you in person,

00:00:29.362 --> 00:00:31.431 line:92%
and that time was in an airport.

00:00:31.431 --> 00:00:34.267 align:start size:94% position:6%
And while I feel you were happ
to see me,

00:00:34.267 --> 00:00:37.270 align:start size:94% position:6%
you were far happier
to see my dog.

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:38.104 line:92%
-Well, as a matter of fact

00:00:38.104 --> 00:00:39.672 align:start size:94% position:6%
I just found out
you're on Instagram.

00:00:39.672 --> 00:00:44.377 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because up until now,
I've been following your dog

00:00:44.377 --> 00:00:47.447 size:84% position:42% line:92%
You're also a presence.

00:00:47.447 --> 00:00:50.550 size:84% position:42%
-Yeah, she's got a real
social-media following.

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:54.487 size:88% position:44%
This is a video that you
and Sarah Paulson took,

00:00:54.487 --> 00:00:56.189 line:92%
right, that we're gonna show

00:00:56.189 --> 00:00:57.323 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes, I believe so.

00:00:57.323 --> 00:00:58.958 align:start size:94% position:6%
The fastest tail wagger
in history.

00:00:58.958 --> 00:01:01.561 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Here it is. I mean,
obviously she's fan of yours

00:01:01.561 --> 00:01:03.096 line:92%
Look how Frisbee reacted.

00:01:03.096 --> 00:01:05.198 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Hello, hello.

00:01:05.198 --> 00:01:10.003 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Hello. Hello. Hi.

00:01:10.003 --> 00:01:12.539 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Oh, my goodness.

00:01:12.539 --> 00:01:15.442 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Hi.

00:01:18.812 --> 00:01:19.979 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:19.979 --> 00:01:22.315 align:start size:94% position:6%
When I told her you were
coming on tonight,

00:01:22.315 --> 00:01:24.984
she waved the tail, knocked over
a glass of water.

00:01:24.984 --> 00:01:25.752 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It was a mess.

00:01:25.752 --> 00:01:28.621 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know, we actually
go to that page

00:01:28.621 --> 00:01:30.924 align:start size:94% position:6%
and look at pictures of he
every so often.

00:01:30.924 --> 00:01:33.626 align:start size:94% position:6%
Very soothing.
She's so darling.

00:01:33.626 --> 00:01:35.528 line:92%
She's the most delicious dog

00:01:35.528 --> 00:01:37.363 align:start size:94% position:6%
-She's going to be so happ
to hear this,

00:01:37.363 --> 00:01:38.231 line:92%
because ever since we had kids

00:01:38.231 --> 00:01:40.733 align:start size:94% position:6%
she feel like she's not gettin
this level of attention.

00:01:40.733 --> 00:01:42.735 align:start size:94% position:6%
-My favorite picture of he
is when she's on the --

00:01:42.735 --> 00:01:48.708
it's from behind the couch, an
you just see her head just tilt.

00:01:48.708 --> 00:01:50.910 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Beautiful big room.

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:55.515 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You and Sarah just got a do
through this time

00:01:55.515 --> 00:01:56.783 line:92%
that I think a lot of people

00:01:56.783 --> 00:01:59.352 align:start size:94% position:6%
wisely have chosen
canine companionship

00:01:59.352 --> 00:02:00.687 line:92%
during this difficult year

00:02:00.687 --> 00:02:01.821 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-Yes, it's wonderful.

00:02:01.821 --> 00:02:04.424 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's a dog park right
catty-corner from our house.

00:02:04.424 --> 00:02:06.826 size:75% position:38%
And most of the dogs
being walked there

00:02:06.826 --> 00:02:07.560 size:84% position:42% line:92%
are new to that family.

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:11.264
They're puppies and young dogs
and they have been rescue --

00:02:11.264 --> 00:02:12.398 line:92%
They're almost all rescue dogs

00:02:12.398 --> 00:02:15.335 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's a thing in
this pandemic, I'm sure,

00:02:15.335 --> 00:02:16.302 size:78% position:39% line:92%
all over the country.

00:02:16.302 --> 00:02:17.737 line:92%
There's lots of new puppies.

00:02:17.737 --> 00:02:19.739 align:start size:94% position:6%
And not only that,
but these young dogs

00:02:19.739 --> 00:02:23.042
have had an unusual amount
of time with their parents

00:02:23.042 --> 00:02:24.410 line:92%
because most people are home

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:28.381
So, it's a great beginning for
millions and millions of dogs.

00:02:28.381 --> 00:02:31.251
-Did you guys become fast
friends, you and the dog?

00:02:31.251 --> 00:02:33.620 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did you take to each other
immediately?

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:34.654 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh, yes.

00:02:34.654 --> 00:02:36.322 align:start size:94% position:6%
Not as darling as Frisbee
in a way

00:02:36.322 --> 00:02:39.159 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause she has
her standoffish ways.

00:02:39.159 --> 00:02:43.096 align:start size:94% position:6%
She's a mixed bag,
as we all are.

00:02:43.096 --> 00:02:44.464 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Very fair.

00:02:44.464 --> 00:02:46.866 align:start size:94% position:6%
You've had a lot
going on this year,

00:02:46.866 --> 00:02:48.434 line:92%
which is a strange thing to have

00:02:48.434 --> 00:02:52.172
at a time when you also can'
go out and promote it in person.

00:02:52.172 --> 00:02:56.109 align:start size:94% position:6%
You have this film "Hollywood"
with Ryan Murphy,

00:02:56.109 --> 00:02:57.343 size:84% position:42% line:92%
the "Bill &amp; Ted" movie.

00:02:57.343 --> 00:03:01.514 align:start size:94% position:6%
Have you enjoyed not having to
leave the house for press,

00:03:01.514 --> 00:03:03.483 align:start size:94% position:6%
or have you found it difficult
-Not really.

00:03:03.483 --> 00:03:06.452
First of all, I mean, it's bee
a frightening year, hasn't it?

00:03:06.452 --> 00:03:09.589 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, we've all been
in an odd emotional state.

00:03:09.589 --> 00:03:11.124 line:92%
And so you retreat to your home.

00:03:11.124 --> 00:03:13.092 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, you have to stay
in your home.

00:03:13.092 --> 00:03:15.261 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it should feel safe,
of course.

00:03:15.261 --> 00:03:17.130 line:92%
You have to go on talk shows

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:18.431 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you have to do
a lot of press.

00:03:18.431 --> 00:03:21.935
I've had like five things have
opened -- or five or six things.

00:03:21.935 --> 00:03:26.439 align:start size:94% position:6%
And to be in your house
seeking safety and comfort

00:03:26.439 --> 00:03:28.007 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then having to
get your slap on

00:03:28.007 --> 00:03:31.711 align:start size:94% position:6%
and appear on television
is a very strange experience

00:03:31.711 --> 00:03:32.712 line:92%
'cause there's no place safe

00:03:32.712 --> 00:03:35.682
Also, I never wear makeup at all
during this whole year,

00:03:35.682 --> 00:03:37.283 size:78% position:39%
except when I'm doing
something like this.

00:03:37.283 --> 00:03:40.220 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I put makeup on
and I see myself,

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:41.020 line:92%
and I look like, you know,

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:44.757 align:start size:94% position:6%
an ancient hooker
still working in Vegas.

00:03:44.757 --> 00:03:47.794 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's a shock from
what I usually --

00:03:47.794 --> 00:03:49.762 align:start size:94% position:6%
-As long as you're
still working.

00:03:49.762 --> 00:03:50.964 line:92%
That's the important thing

00:03:50.964 --> 00:03:52.232 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I'm working, baby.

00:03:52.232 --> 00:03:54.033 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm about to go to work
on something, too.

00:03:54.033 --> 00:03:56.703 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm gonna be working in
Pittsburgh for like six weeks.

00:03:56.703 --> 00:03:59.639 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's gonna be something
during this pandemic.

00:03:59.639 --> 00:04:02.742 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's great and, you know,
obviously very exciting.

00:04:02.742 --> 00:04:04.844 line:92%
Another thing that was exciting,

00:04:04.844 --> 00:04:07.046 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I know it's sort of
put on pause now,

00:04:07.046 --> 00:04:11.451 size:84% position:42%
you played Ann Richards
in a play called "Ann."

00:04:11.451 --> 00:04:12.785 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
That was your idea.

00:04:12.785 --> 00:04:16.823
And you were about to do it in
California for the first time.

00:04:16.823 --> 00:04:18.558 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is that --
Of the roles you've played

00:04:18.558 --> 00:04:21.461 align:start size:94% position:6%
does that one hold
a special place in your heart?

00:04:21.461 --> 00:04:24.631 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That one really, you know
it wasn't a job.

00:04:24.631 --> 00:04:25.565 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It was a mission.

00:04:25.565 --> 00:04:27.767 align:start size:94% position:6%
I didn't think of it
like an idea.

00:04:27.767 --> 00:04:31.471
It really flooded over me
truly like an inspiration,

00:04:31.471 --> 00:04:33.973 align:start size:94% position:6%
the only thing that ever
happened like that in my life.

00:04:33.973 --> 00:04:36.776 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was in my 60s.
So that's really remarkable.

00:04:36.776 --> 00:04:39.812 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I created --
It was a very long process

00:04:39.812 --> 00:04:40.813 size:81% position:41% line:92%
years in the creation,

00:04:40.813 --> 00:04:42.882 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I did it
all over the country

00:04:42.882 --> 00:04:44.350 line:92%
and on Broadway, certainly

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:45.285 size:84% position:42% line:92%
And it was, you know --

00:04:45.285 --> 00:04:50.189 align:start size:94% position:6%
I wanted that great
American patriot to be known

00:04:50.189 --> 00:04:53.693
and still around to inspir
people, because she does.

00:04:53.693 --> 00:04:56.296 size:84% position:42%
So that is my greatest
achievement of my life.

00:04:56.296 --> 00:04:58.564 align:start size:94% position:6%
That is for sure, and I don'
think of it as a job.

00:04:58.564 --> 00:05:02.735 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I know you were lucky enoug
to get know Ann Richards,

00:05:02.735 --> 00:05:04.804 line:92%
who was the governor of Texas.

00:05:04.804 --> 00:05:06.239 line:92%
And you also then had to do,

00:05:06.239 --> 00:05:09.475
I think when you decided thi
was a play you were going to do,

00:05:09.475 --> 00:05:11.611 align:start size:94% position:6%
a great amount of research
on her.

00:05:11.611 --> 00:05:13.980 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, the research
is where I got it all.

00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:15.515 align:start size:94% position:6%
And for some reason,
I don't know,

00:05:15.515 --> 00:05:19.152 align:start size:94% position:6%
everybody around her felt
that I could do this.

00:05:19.152 --> 00:05:20.620 line:92%
And the doors were opened.

00:05:20.620 --> 00:05:21.888 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I've become
very good friends

00:05:21.888 --> 00:05:25.491 align:start size:94% position:6%
with lot of her closest people
who were friends

00:05:25.491 --> 00:05:27.760 align:start size:94% position:6%
and also part
of her administration,

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:28.361 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
one and the same.

00:05:28.361 --> 00:05:31.864 size:81% position:41%
And I really deep dive
for about three years

00:05:31.864 --> 00:05:32.832 line:92%
before I put pen to paper.

00:05:32.832 --> 00:05:38.504 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I just hoped that if I
created like a hologram of her

00:05:38.504 --> 00:05:43.176
some of the inspiration woul
come along with it, and it did

00:05:43.176 --> 00:05:44.877 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so when people see me
on the street

00:05:44.877 --> 00:05:46.913 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they compliment me on that
it's so great

00:05:46.913 --> 00:05:48.581 size:81% position:41%
'cause they don't say,
"You were so great."

00:05:48.581 --> 00:05:51.951 align:start size:94% position:6%
They saw, "I saw your play
I was so inspired.

00:05:51.951 --> 00:05:53.953 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
She was so great."

00:05:53.953 --> 00:05:55.788 line:92%
That's exactly what I wanted

00:05:55.788 --> 00:05:56.589 size:78% position:39% line:92%
So, I was very lucky.

00:05:56.589 --> 00:05:59.392 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Did you do it --
Did it premiere in Texas?

00:05:59.392 --> 00:06:00.660 align:start size:94% position:6%
Was that the first place
you did it?

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:04.931 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, we did it
in Galveston, Texas,

00:06:04.931 --> 00:06:07.367 align:start size:94% position:6%
the first time
at the opera house there.

00:06:07.367 --> 00:06:09.435 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we did it at the Paramount
in Austin.

00:06:09.435 --> 00:06:11.971 align:start size:94% position:6%
Then we did it at the Empire
in San Antonio.

00:06:11.971 --> 00:06:15.108 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then we did it at
the great Shubert in Chicago

00:06:15.108 --> 00:06:16.309 line:92%
which is great theater town.

00:06:16.309 --> 00:06:18.544 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then we did it
at the Kennedy Center.

00:06:18.544 --> 00:06:19.846 line:92%
That was a great invitation.

00:06:19.846 --> 00:06:22.415 size:88% position:44%
That was truly thrilling
on the main stage there.

00:06:22.415 --> 00:06:24.117 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then we did it
at Lincoln Center.

00:06:24.117 --> 00:06:28.388 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Were the stakes higher for yo
doing it in Texas

00:06:28.388 --> 00:06:29.622 align:start size:94% position:6%
for the first time,
the place where people

00:06:29.622 --> 00:06:31.591 align:start size:94% position:6%
were maybe the most familiar
with her, obviously?

00:06:31.591 --> 00:06:33.526 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I was terrified.
And I got much better.

00:06:33.526 --> 00:06:36.596 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I worked with
a dialect person, always.

00:06:36.596 --> 00:06:40.633 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was also constantly
refining the play

00:06:40.633 --> 00:06:41.267 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
and working on it.

00:06:41.267 --> 00:06:44.871 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I would learn a great dea
every run.

00:06:44.871 --> 00:06:46.606 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I also had to
always shorten it,

00:06:46.606 --> 00:06:48.107 align:start size:94% position:6%
because you have to
keep it very tight

00:06:48.107 --> 00:06:49.475 line:92%
as we headed towards Broadway.

00:06:49.475 --> 00:06:52.478 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so when I opened it,
I was terrified

00:06:52.478 --> 00:06:55.681 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause I was opening it
in her backyard.

00:06:55.681 --> 00:06:57.116 size:78% position:39% line:92%
And the play started,

00:06:57.116 --> 00:07:00.319 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I literally heard a gasp
in the audience.

00:07:00.319 --> 00:07:03.523 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that's Paul Huntley's wig,
I think, got that.

00:07:03.523 --> 00:07:06.959 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it was open sesame
from there on.

00:07:06.959 --> 00:07:10.696 align:start size:94% position:6%
For some reason they just said
"Yeah, we're buying this."

00:07:10.696 --> 00:07:11.964 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-That's so exciting.

00:07:11.964 --> 00:07:14.267
And that's such wonderful
feedback to get from fans.

00:07:14.267 --> 00:07:19.705 align:start size:94% position:6%
I also want to ask, becaus
you had such a diverse career,

00:07:19.705 --> 00:07:20.640 line:92%
you know, a storied career

00:07:20.640 --> 00:07:22.508 align:start size:94% position:6%
that's ranged everywhere
from drama to comedy.

00:07:22.508 --> 00:07:26.646
Is there something specific that
people most approach you about

00:07:26.646 --> 00:07:27.580 line:92%
when they see you on the street?

00:07:27.580 --> 00:07:31.484
-"Legally Blonde" is probabl
the most because of that line.

00:07:31.484 --> 00:07:34.253 align:start size:94% position:6%
"If you're gonna let
one stupid prick ruin" --

00:07:34.253 --> 00:07:36.389 size:75% position:38%
I can't even say it.
That wonderful line.

00:07:36.389 --> 00:07:39.192 align:start size:94% position:6%
"If you let one stupid prick
ruin your life,

00:07:39.192 --> 00:07:40.593 align:start size:94% position:6%
you're not the girl
I thought you were."

00:07:40.593 --> 00:07:42.595 align:start size:94% position:6%
Something like that.
People love that.

00:07:42.595 --> 00:07:45.531 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It is certainly
a multigenerational

00:07:45.531 --> 00:07:46.866 size:78% position:39% line:92%
good piece of advice.

00:07:46.866 --> 00:07:47.800 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-It was a great role.

00:07:47.800 --> 00:07:51.070 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's wonderful to play
a great teacher, which she was

00:07:51.070 --> 00:07:54.006 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, it's been such an honor
to have you here.

00:07:54.006 --> 00:07:57.610 size:84% position:42%
I really do appreciate
you giving us the time.

00:07:57.610 --> 00:07:59.745 size:81% position:41%
And thank you so much.
-It was my pleasure.

00:07:59.745 --> 00:08:03.649 align:start size:94% position:6%
And would you please tell
Frisbee she's a very good girl

00:08:03.649 --> 00:08:06.252
-I might just play the tap
'cause it's so much better

00:08:06.252 --> 00:08:09.555 align:start size:94% position:6%
coming from you
than it is from me.

